{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489489c9e2938b0738fed20a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4zpq71","claim:pm-fr10t8","claim:pm-gh1580","claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-fr10t8","lineage:pm-yql1","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-4zpq71+pm-fr10t8+pm-gh1580+pm-gh1647","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4zpq71","claim:pm-fr10t8","claim:pm-gh1580","claim:pm-gh1647","lineage:pm-fr10t8","lineage:pm-yql1","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-8s53lj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Bare pm comments / pm notes reads keep the oldest page when output must be bounded, withholding the newest entries (GH-1605 fixed this for history only)"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Measured on pm 2026.11.1 against this repository's tracker. When a bare read of an item's comments or notes has to be bounded, it returns the OLDEST page and withholds the newest entries:\n\n- pm comments pm-7zs0 --json (261 comments) returns 28 entries dated 2026-06-10..2026-06-30 with has_more: true and an output cursor. The newest entry (2026-11-01) is reachable only through --limit N (\"Return only latest n comments\") or by following about ten cursors.\n- pm notes pm-doxj --json returns 28 notes dated 2026-06-07..2026-07-10, while pm notes pm-doxj --limit 1 shows the newest note is from 2026-09-28.\n\nThis is the same defect GH-1605 (pm-gh1605) fixed for pm history: a default read should preserve the recent tail when it must truncate. The annotation surfaces did not get that fix. It has a real cost. While recording a release-health checkpoint, an agent verified its new comment with pm comments <id> --json | .comments[-1], saw a June entry, concluded the write had failed, and posted a duplicate that then had to be deleted with --delete. On long-lived living-map items, the newest evidence is exactly what the default view hides.\n\nScope: the default bounded selection for pm comments and pm notes (and pm learnings, if it shares the reader). Explicit --limit already selects the latest N."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","annotations","context-management","output-contract","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A bare pm comments <id> and pm notes <id> read that must be bounded returns the newest entries (the recent tail) and reports the omitted older entries with a cursor that continues backwards; pm learnings follows the same rule; Regression test: an item with more annotations than the default bound returns the latest entry on a bare read in JSON and TOON; Command reference documents the bounded default for annotation reads"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A bare annotation read on a long-lived item always includes the most recent comment or note."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm comments pm-7zs0 --json returns 28 comments from June 2026 out of 261; the 2026-11-01 entry is withheld."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-6vfg","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1605","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T11:19:29.712Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"c4687295370208c54ff810ec1104ef23c978ae0e799a7a646dd60ad4e97d0fb9","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"68cc46bec7f51f4b3e98f5e39c03495bf35c904005bb9d5422bc83064002d3d0"}
